  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Interpreting the fraction as division, we can write our expression as\n\n$$\n(5\\,÷\\,6)\\times (12\\,÷\\,5).\n$$\n\nWe use parentheses to make it easier to read.\n\nSince our expression contains multiplication and division only, we can write an equivalent expression by swapping the $÷\\,6$ and the $÷\\,5$:\n\n$$\n(5\\,÷\\,5)\\times (12\\,÷\\,6)\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the $5÷5$ and $12÷6$ as fractions:\n\n$$\n\\frac{5}{5}\\times \\frac{12}{6}\n$$",
